\lceil x\rceil+\lfloor x\rfloor+x&=4.8\\
(n+1)+n+(n+r)&=4.8\\
n&=1,\frac{1}{3}
\end{align*}If $n=\frac{1}{3}$, then $x=\frac{1}{3}+r$. If $\frac{1}{3}<r<\frac{1}{2}$, then that value of $x$ is not possible. If $r=\frac{1}{3}$, which implies $x=1\frac{1}{3}\equiv\frac{1}{2}\frac{1}{3}$, the original equation isn't true. So $r=\frac{1}{2}$, and $x=1+\frac{1/2}=\boxed{1\frac{1}{2}}$. </think> <answer> 1\frac{1}{2} </answer>

